## Features

- **Real-time meter dashboard** — live kWh balance, daily average usage, depletion forecast.
- **Tenant MVP dashboard** — one screen answering "how much electricity do I have", "when will it run out", "what am I spending", plus a Buy Tokens CTA, weekly budget and energy-saving tips.
- **Instant token vending** — buy tokens via M-Pesa, Airtel Money or bank transfer; tokens are generated and recorded instantly.
- **Token & payment history** — every token and transaction is stored in the database, with search, filter, copy, CSV download and print/PDF backup.
- **Send power to your meter (WiFi / Bluetooth)** — load a bought token straight onto your prepaid meter without typing the 20-digit code. Uses the Web Bluetooth API when available, with a simulated delivery fallback for development.
- **Usage analytics** — daily/weekly/monthly consumption and estimated cost charts from recorded telemetry.
- **AI-style predictions** — run-out forecast with confidence level plus "how long does a KSh 200/500/1,000/2,000 token last" estimates.
- **Energy Intelligence hub** — a combined AI energy coach, appliance-level insights and monthly budget planner per meter. It detects week-over-week usage jumps, explains what probably caused them (e.g. a left-on geyser), estimates each registered appliance's share of the bill, projects your full-month spend at the current pace ("likely to spend KSh 3,240 this month") and warns you before you exceed the budget you set.
- **Low-balance alerts** — push / email / SMS rules with configurable thresholds.
- **Smart notification copy** — dashboard warnings phrase the forecast naturally: “at this rate your power is estimated to run out Thursday at 7:00 PM.”
- **Buy-time cost simulator** — on the Buy Tokens page, slide your expected usage to preview monthly spend, the kWh a token delivers and how many days it will last before you pay.
- **Emergency power transfer** — send token value straight to another registered meter from Token History, for when a family member or neighbour runs out.
- **Power Pools (shared electricity wallet)** — groups of people (families, housemates, hostels, small businesses) pool money around a shared meter. Members join by invite code, contribute KSh via M-Pesa/Airtel/bank, and authorised members buy tokens from the pooled balance. Roles and permissions gate who can manage members or buy tokens; a per-pool ledger records every contribution and purchase plus each member's share.
- **Landlord intelligence (Unit Insights)** — compare every rental unit side-by-side (usage, spend, week-over-week trend, remaining balance) and an unusual-usage engine flags sudden spikes, persistently very-high loads and suspicious inactivity — patterns that point to theft, a running geyser or a new heavy load. Each flag comes with an explanation and a suggested action.
- **Automatic expense reports** — one-click monthly statements (token purchases per meter, units bought, spend and average rate) with CSV export for tenants and landlords, plus portfolio totals.
- **Savings Hub** — reduction goals ("cut my bill from KSh 3,000 to KSh 2,500") tracked against live usage, weekly energy-saving challenges with points and a platform-wide leaderboard, and a carbon footprint estimate (kg CO₂/month and tree-equivalent offset) derived from consumption.
- **Merchant (vendor) mode** — authorised agents, kiosks and shops sell electricity tokens. Merchants top up a KSh float via M-Pesa/Airtel/bank and vend tokens straight onto a customer's meter account; every top-up and sale is recorded in a sales ledger. Admins can approve or suspend vendor accounts.
- **Offline Kit** — save a snapshot of your balance, run-out forecast, tokens and recent payments onto the device, and keep seeing it when the internet drops.
- **Energy Marketplace** — an energy-saving product catalogue (solar, LEDs, smart plugs, efficient appliances, audits) where the AI recommends items with reasons drawn from your appliance mix and spend: e.g. “your water heater is ~31% of usage — a solar water heater could cut that demand.”
- **Power reserve** — set aside part of your balance as an emergency reserve; the dashboard shows balance vs available vs reserved, and you release the reserve only when you truly need it.
- **Power Help (“I need power”)** — public emergency requests; anyone can fulfil one and PowerSmart issues a token straight onto the requester's meter, recording the helper. Each user can also ask for help and track/cancel their own requests.
- **Green Energy Score** — a monthly 0–100 efficiency score (grade + usage trend + carbon + challenge points) computed from the meter, shown on the Savings Hub.
- **Receipt scanner** — paste a KPLC SMS/paper receipt in Token History and PowerSmart extracts the 20-digit token, amount, units and date, then saves it to your history (duplicates rejected) so no token is ever lost.
- **Voice Power Assistant** — ask your meter questions with your voice (Web Speech API) or by typing: balance, run-out estimate, usage, and guided purchases — with spoken replies you can mute.
- **Neighborhood energy challenges** — set your estate/area and your challenge points start counting toward a local leaderboard that ranks neighborhoods (e.g. Kilimani vs South B) by savings effort.
- **Auto top-up** — automatically buy tokens when the balance drops below a threshold.
- **Role-based portals** — separate experiences for **Tenant**, **Landlord** and **Admin**, each with its own login.
- **Dedicated admin console** — global stats, user list, meter fleet, token ledger, payment audit trail and vendor approvals (activate / suspend merchant accounts).
- **Security-first** — bcrypt password hashing, signed expiring JWTs, rate-limited auth, security headers, input validation, webhook secrets and RBAC.

## Tech stack

| Layer    | Technology |
|----------|-----------|
| Backend  | Go (`net/http`), PostgreSQL (`jackc/pgx`), JWT (`golang-jwt`), bcrypt |
| Frontend | Plain HTML + CSS + JavaScript, served separately via Vite (dev) or any static host (prod) |
| Optional | React + Vite prototype under `frontend/src/` (dev only, not required to run) |

## Project structure

```
powersmart-kenya/
├── backend/
│   ├── main.go                  # Server entry point + route wiring
│   ├── .env.example             # Copy to .env and fill in values
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── database.go          # PostgreSQL connection + table migrations
│   │   ├── env.go               # Environment helpers
│   │   └── seed.go              # Admin account seeding (env-driven)
│   ├── handlers/                # HTTP handlers per resource
│   ├── middleware/              # Auth, CORS, rate-limit, security headers, webhooks
│   ├── model/                   # Data structures
│   ├── repositories/            # Database access layer
│   ├── service/                 # Business logic
│   └── utils/                   # JWT, validation, responses, KP validator
└── frontend/
    ├── index.html               # Landing / marketing page (served at "/")
    ├── app.html                 # React app entry (customer portal: login/register/dashboard)
    ├── src/                     # React + Vite + Tailwind app (main customer experience)
    │   ├── App.tsx              # Session guard + role routing
    │   ├── screens/             # Auth.tsx, Dashboard.tsx
    │   ├── components/          # LiveGauge, ApplianceSliders, TokenVault
    │   └── services/api.ts      # Typed API client + session helpers
    ├── public/                  # Static assets (copied to dist/ on build)
    │   ├── admin-login.html     # Administrator login (separate)
    │   ├── admin-dashboard.html # Admin console (legacy vanilla JS)
    │   ├── tenant-dashboard.html, landlord.html  # Legacy portals
    │   ├── app.js               # Shared API client + session guards (legacy pages)
    │   ├── config.js            # window.POWERSMART_API (baked by build.sh in prod)
    │   └── css/                 # Design system (portal.css, landing.css)
    ├── build.sh                 # Production build (bakes $VITE_API_URL into config.js)
    └── vite.config.ts           # Dev server + /api proxy to the Go backend (multi-page build)
```

## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- **Go 1.25+** — <https://go.dev/dl/>
- **PostgreSQL 14+** — local install, Docker, or a managed host (Neon / Supabase / Render)

### 1. Install & build the backend

```bash
cd backend
go build -o app .
```

### 2. Configure the environment

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Edit `.env` and set at least:

```env
APP_ENV=development
PORT=8080
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string-at-least-32-chars
```

> Generate a strong secret with: `openssl rand -hex 32`

### 3. (Optional) Create the administrator account

Admins are **never** created through public registration. Set these in `.env` and the server seeds the account on startup:

```env
ADMIN_NAME=Super Administrator
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=a-strong-and-unique-password
```

### 4. Run the server

```bash
cd backend
go run .            # or: ./app
```

The server:

- Starts on `http://localhost:8080` (change with `PORT`)
- Connects to PostgreSQL (`DB_DSN`, default `postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/powersmart`) and creates all tables automatically
- Exposes the JSON API under `/api/*` only — it does **not** serve the frontend

### 5. Run the frontend (separate process)

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev         # Vite dev server on http://localhost:3000
```

The Vite dev server proxies every `/api` request to the backend on `:8080`
(see `frontend/vite.config.ts`), so the browser only talks to `http://localhost:3000`
and no CORS is involved.

For production, build the static site with `npm run build` and serve `frontend/dist`
from any static host, setting `window.POWERSMART_API` (or the `VITE_API_URL` build
env var) to your backend API URL.

### 6. Open the portal

| Page | URL |
|------|-----|
| Landing / marketing page | `http://localhost:3000/` |
| Customer login / register | `http://localhost:3000/app.html` |
| Admin login | `http://localhost:3000/admin-login.html` |

**Quick demo flow**

1. Open `http://localhost:3000/` → **Create account** → fill the form (role: Tenant or Landlord, meter account = 8–12 digits).
2. You are signed in automatically and redirected to the matching dashboard.
3. Go to the **Top-up** tab, pick an amount and channel, buy a token.
4. Open `http://localhost:3000/admin-login.html`, sign in with the `ADMIN_EMAIL` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` you configured — explore users, meters, tokens and transactions.

## Demo data

To explore every dashboard with realistic data, seed the database (idempotent — run it again later and it skips):

```bash
cd backend
go run ./cmd/seed
```

Demo logins (password `DemoPass1`):

| Role | Email | What to look at |
|------|-------|-----------------|
| Tenant | `emma@demo.com` | Energy Intelligence, Savings Hub, Power Pools (owner) |
| Pool member | `brian@demo.com` | Power Pools (contribute / buy) |
| Landlord | `landlord@demo.com` | Unit Insights — Unit 2 is flagged as spiking, Vendor Mode |
| Tenant | `grace@demo.com` | Savings leaderboard rival |

## Configuration

All configuration is via environment variables (see `backend/.env.example`).

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | `production` enables HSTS and enforces a strong `JWT_SECRET` |
| `PORT` | `8080` | HTTP port |
| `JWT_SECRET` | *(auto random in dev)* | JWT signing key; **required ≥ 32 chars in production** |
| `DB_DRIVER` | `postgres` | Database driver |
| `DB_DSN` | `postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/powersmart?sslmode=disable` | PostgreSQL connection string |
| `DATABASE_URL` | *(overrides DB_DSN)* | Full connection string used on managed hosts (Render/Heroku) |
| `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | *(empty = allow all in dev)* | Comma-separated allowed browser origins (set to your frontend domain(s) in production) |
| `KP_API_URL` | *(empty = format check)* | Kenya Power account lookup API |
| `ADMIN_NAME` | `System Administrator` | Admin account name (seed) |
| `ADMIN_EMAIL` | — | Admin account email (seed) |
| `ADMIN_PASSWORD` | — | Admin account password (seed) |
| `MPESA_*` | — | M-Pesa Daraja credentials & callback URL |
| `MPESA_ENV` | `sandbox` | `sandbox` or `production` — picks the Safaricom Daraja endpoint (`MPESA_API_BASE` overrides it) |
| `AIRTEL_*` | — | Airtel Money API key & callback URL |
| `BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER` | — | Virtual bank account details |
| `MPESA_CALLBACK_SECRET` | — | Shared secret for M-Pesa callbacks |
| `AIRTEL_CALLBACK_SECRET` | — | Shared secret for Airtel callbacks |

## API overview

Public endpoints:

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | Create a tenant/landlord account |
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | Sign in (any role) |
| POST | `/api/auth/admin-login` | Admin-only sign in (rejects other roles) |
| GET | `/api/health` | Health check |

Protected endpoints (JWT `Authorization: Bearer <token>`):

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Current user profile |
| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Session discard (stateless) |
| GET | `/api/meter` | Live meter status |
| POST | `/api/meter/telemetry` | Record a meter reading |
| GET | `/api/meter/prediction` | Depletion forecast |
| GET | `/api/meter/usage` | Today / week / month usage + 30-day series (Usage dashboard) |
| GET | `/api/energy/intel` | Energy Intelligence bundle: coach insights, appliance model + spend/budget forecast |
| PUT | `/api/energy/budget` | Set the monthly spend target (`monthly_budget_ksh`, optional `meter_id`) |
| POST | `/api/energy/appliances` | Register an appliance (`name`, `watts`, `hours_per_day`) |
| PUT | `/api/energy/appliances/{id}` | Edit an appliance (name / watts / hours per day) |
| DELETE | `/api/energy/appliances/{id}` | Remove an appliance |
| POST | `/api/pools` | Create a Power Pool around a meter I own |
| GET | `/api/pools` | List pools I belong to |
| GET | `/api/pools/{id}` | Pool detail: members + contribution/purchase ledger |
| POST | `/api/pools/join` | Join a pool with an invite code |
| POST | `/api/pools/{id}/contributions` | Add money to the pool wallet |
| POST | `/api/pools/{id}/purchase` | Buy a token from the pooled balance |
| POST | `/api/pools/{id}/members` | Add a member by email (owner/admin) |
| PATCH | `/api/pools/{id}/members/{memberId}` | Change a member's role/permissions |
| DELETE | `/api/pools/{id}/members/{memberId}` | Remove a member / leave the pool |
| GET | `/api/insights` | Landlord unit comparison with anomaly flags |
| GET | `/api/reports/monthly?month=YYYY-MM` | Monthly token-spend statement per meter |
| GET/POST | `/api/goals` | List / create a savings reduction goal |
| POST | `/api/goals/{id}/complete` | Mark a goal achieved |
| DELETE | `/api/goals/{id}` | Remove a goal |
| GET | `/api/challenges` | Weekly energy-saving challenges + my status |
| POST | `/api/challenges/{key}/claim` | Verify and claim a challenge's points |
| GET | `/api/challenges/leaderboard` | Top scorers + my standing |
| GET | `/api/challenges/neighborhoods` | Neighborhood challenge leaderboard |
| PUT | `/api/profile/neighborhood` | Set my estate/area for local challenges |
| GET | `/api/impact/carbon` | CO₂ estimate for my primary meter |
| GET | `/api/impact/score` | Monthly green energy score (0–100 + grade) |
| GET/PUT | `/api/meter/reserve` | Read / set the emergency power reserve (kWh) |
| POST | `/api/meter/reserve/release` | Unlock the emergency reserve |
| POST | `/api/power-requests` | Ask the community for emergency power |
| GET | `/api/power-requests` | Open requests + my requests |
| POST | `/api/power-requests/{id}/fulfill` | Send power to a requester |
| POST | `/api/power-requests/{id}/cancel` | Cancel my open request |
| POST | `/api/merchant/apply` | Register my business as a PowerSmart vendor |
| GET | `/api/merchant/me` | My vendor profile, float and recent sales |
| POST | `/api/merchant/float` | Top up my vending float |
| POST | `/api/merchant/vend` | Sell a token to a customer's meter account |
| GET | `/api/marketplace` | Product catalogue + AI recommendations for my meter |
| GET | `/api/admin/merchants` | List all vendor accounts (admin) |
| POST | `/api/admin/merchants/{id}/status` | Approve / suspend a vendor (admin) |
| PUT | `/api/meter/settings` | Auto top-up settings |
| GET | `/api/tokens` | Token history |
| POST | `/api/tokens/buy` | Purchase a token |
| POST | `/api/tokens/import` | Add a token from a receipt/SMS (duplicates rejected) |
| POST | `/api/tokens/{id}/push-bluetooth` | Push token to meter (`?action=request\|confirm\|fail&method=wifi\|bluetooth`) |
| DELETE | `/api/tokens/{id}` | Remove a token from history |
| GET | `/api/transactions` | Payment history |
| GET/POST/PUT/DELETE | `/api/alerts...` | Alert rules |
| POST | `/api/payments/{channel}/initiate` | Initiate M-Pesa / Airtel / bank payment |
| GET | `/api/payments/config` | Which live payment channels are configured (drives real STK vs simulated buys) |

Admin-only endpoints (role `admin` required):

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/admin/stats` | Global operational counts |
| GET | `/api/admin/users` | All registered accounts |
| GET | `/api/admin/meters` | All meters with owners |
| GET | `/api/admin/tokens` | Recent 50 tokens platform-wide |
| GET | `/api/admin/transactions` | Recent 50 payments platform-wide |

Public callbacks (payment providers):

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/payments/mpesa/callback` | Safaricom M-Pesa callback |
| POST | `/api/payments/airtel/callback` | Airtel Money callback |

## Database

PostgreSQL tables are created automatically on first run (`backend/config/database.go`):

- `users` — accounts (id, name, email, phone, password hash, meter_account, meter_number, role, created_at)
- `meters` — meter state (units_remaining, daily_avg_units, auto_topup, thresholds)
- `usage_history` — point-in-time readings for forecasts
- `tokens` — purchased token records
- `transactions` — payment records
- `alerts` — alert rules
- `energy_budgets` — per-meter monthly spend targets (Energy Intelligence)
- `appliances` — registered household appliances for consumption modelling
- `power_pools` — shared electricity wallets (name, meter, invite code, creator)
- `pool_members` — who belongs to each pool plus roles/permissions
- `pool_contributions` — money added to a pool wallet
- `pool_expenses` — token purchases paid from a pool wallet
- `savings_goals` — monthly-spend reduction goals per meter
- `challenge_points` — weekly energy-saving challenge points per user
- `merchant_profiles` — vendor businesses (name, status, owner)
- `merchant_ledger` — float top-ups and token sales per merchant
- `marketplace_products` — energy-saving product catalogue for recommendations
- `meter_reserves` — emergency kWh reserved per meter
- `power_requests` — public “I need power” help requests

## Security

- **Passwords** — bcrypt-hashed, never stored or serialised in plain text.
- **Sessions** — signed HS256 JWTs with issuer/audience/expiry; validated on every protected call.
- **JWT secret enforcement** — the server refuses to start in production without a strong `JWT_SECRET`.
- **Rate limiting** — general API limiting plus a stricter limiter on all auth endpoints to slow brute-force attacks.
- **Security headers** — CSP, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `nosniff`, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, HSTS (prod).
- **Input validation** — email format, Kenyan phone format, password strength, name/role checks.
- **Role-based access control** — admin endpoints reject tenant/landlord tokens; the admin login refuses non-admin accounts.
- **Webhook secrets** — optional shared-secret checks on the payment callbacks.
- **CORS** — the API is cross-origin by design (frontend is hosted separately); allow-listed origins are enforced in production.

## Testing

The backend ships with no automated test suite; smoke-test the API directly:

```bash
# Health
curl http://localhost:8080/api/health

# Register a tenant
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"Emma Jane","email":"emma@example.com","phone":"0712345678","password":"StrongPass1","meter_account":"1234567890"}'

# Login
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"emma@example.com","password":"StrongPass1"}'
```

Verify code health:

```bash
cd backend
go vet ./...
go build ./...
```

